---
import ScrollArrow from "@components/global/ScrollArrow.astro";
---

<section id="method" class="w-full bg-[#18181b] text-white py-24 lg:py-32">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 md:px-8">
		<!-- Label -->
		<div class="mb-16 lg:mb-24">
			<span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500 font-mono">The Method</span>
		</div>

		<!-- Two Column Layout -->
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-16">
			<!-- Left Column (Heading) -->
			<div class="lg:col-span-5">
				<h2 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight">
					Every engagement starts with the brand.
				</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column (Body text) -->
			<div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pl-10 space-y-6 font-sans text-lg lg:text-xl font-light text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
				<p>
					Not with a logo or a color palette — with understanding what a business 
					truly stands for, who it serves, and where it's losing ground. That clarity 
					is the foundation for everything we develop.
				</p>
				<p>
					We call it <strong>The Step Back</strong>. When a client comes with a tactical request — 
					a website, a report, a campaign — we pause before executing. We diagnose 
					the real friction first. Then we define the right architecture. Then we build.
				</p>
				<p>
					That's what separates a deliverable from a solution.
				</p>
				<p class="italic">
					We use AI not as a selling point, but as the engine that makes our work 
					faster and more precise — without replacing the thinking.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<ScrollArrow targetId="#projects" upTargetId="#hero" upColor="#e25432" color="#45ccaa" id="method-arrow" />
	</div>
</section>
